81524aa5bc037d66794c239ac6b9d2b4e86"},{"sha":"266aec860248a7c14b00a61dcc9544b4abf66fd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/commits/266aec860248a7c14b00a61dcc9544b4abf66fd2","html_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/commit/266aec860248a7c14b00a61dcc9544b4abf66fd2"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"41671380c2d4c06af1830e56a790f69ddc28e878","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S3/ConceptDynamics/Coding/PrimitiveLifts/FiniteRootFiberCoherence.md","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changes":4,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/e1d4e12fbc1f1f82e5f88362e931a52c778b4374/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FFiniteRootFiberCoherence.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/e1d4e12fbc1f1f82e5f88362e931a52c778b4374/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FFiniteRootFiberCoherence.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FFiniteRootFiberCoherence.md?ref=e1d4e12fbc1f1f82e5f88362e931a52c778b4374","patch":"@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ For q=a/d define F(q)=b_d^a, with integer exponent. To prove F(q+r)=F(q)F(r), us\n \n The theorem asserts existence only. Finite fibers do not imply uniqueness of the resulting homomorphism.\n \n+The same root system and rational_action_of_coherent_roots also apply to a Hausdorff topological group H when every actual root set R_n(h)={x in H | x^n=h} is compact for every n>0. Roots exist in all positive degrees if and only if an algebraic monoid homomorphism phi:Multiplicative Q -> H sends Multiplicative.ofAdd(1:Q) to h. Give each root set its subspace topology and use the continuous power maps R_m(h) -> R_n(h), x -> x^(m/n), for n dividing m. Under the root-existence hypothesis these form a cofiltered system of nonempty compact Hausdorff spaces. Mathlib's TopCat.nonempty_limitCone_of_compact_t2_cofiltered_system supplies compatible roots without requiring onto transition maps. The common cyclic denominator calculation above proves the homomorphism law even for noncommutative H; the converse again uses map_pow.\n+\n+This composition of existing results connects the finite theorem to CompactRootCoherence.exists_all_positive_roots_iff_exists_rat_hom: finite fibers are compact in the discrete group topology, while in a compact Hausdorff group each R_n(h) is closed as the inverse image of {h} under a continuous power map, and hence compact. The compact-root application requires neither finite root sets nor a compact ambient group. Its conclusion is algebraic existence only; it asserts no continuity or uniqueness of the homomorphism, no necessity of root-set compactness, and no literature novelty.\n+\n ## References\n \n - Truth anchor: `D5/S3/ConceptDynamics/Coding/PrimitiveLifts/FiniteRootFiberCoherence.finite_root_fibers_rational_coherence`"},{"sha":"a7ac94762070143760c487658ef26851ffde07f2","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S3/ConceptDynamics/Coding/PrimitiveLifts/FiniteRootFiberCoherence.scribe.cs","status":"modified","additions":23,"deletions":1,"changes":24,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/e1d4e12fbc1f1f82e5f88362e931a52c778b4374/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FFiniteRootFiberCoherence.scribe.cs","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/e1d4e12fbc1f1f82e5f88362e931a52c778b4374/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FFiniteRootFiberCoherence.scribe.cs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FFiniteRootFiberCoherence.scribe.cs?ref=e1d4e12fbc1f1f82e5f88362e931a52c778b4374","patch":"@@ -46,7 +46,29 @@ public DocumentDefinition Create() => DocumentDefinition.Create(ScribeNode.Creat\n                         + \"homomorphism at Multiplicati